@deterred
on-arrival: falklands = 6; thatcher_rating += 1
achievement: deterrence
face-image: img/events/endurance.jpg

= Tension in the South Atlantic

Argentine scrap-metal workers have landed on South Georgia and raised their flag. HMS Endurance, still on station, is ordered to remove them, and the junta in Buenos Aires decides that Britain is not bluffing. The crisis fades within weeks. Most people in Britain never hear of it.

@invasion
on-arrival: falklands = 1; thatcher_rating -= 4; right_dissent += 10
face-image: img/events/stanley_1982.jpg

= Invasion

On 2 April, Argentine forces land on the Falkland Islands. The small garrison of Royal Marines is overwhelmed, and the Governor is flown out. For the first time since 1945, British territory has been seized by a foreign power, eight thousand miles away.

In an emergency Saturday sitting of the Commons, members on every side demand action. Lord Carrington, the Foreign Secretary, offers his resignation.

- @accept_resignation: Accept Carrington's resignation.
- @refuse_resignation: Refuse it.

@accept_resignation
on-arrival: foreign_secretary = "Pym"; right_dissent -= 4
go-to: task_force

Carrington goes, taking responsibility for the Foreign Office's failure. Francis Pym replaces him.

@refuse_resignation
on-arrival: thatcher_rating -= 2; right_dissent += 4
go-to: task_force

You keep Carrington. The backbenches want a head, and if it isn't his it may be someone else's.

@task_force

The First Sea Lord, Sir Henry Leach, says the Navy can assemble a task force within days and retake the islands. Most of your advisers think it is a huge gamble. The Americans would prefer a negotiated settlement.

- @send: Send the task force.
- @negotiate: Negotiate: accept international mediation.

@send
on-arrival: falklands = 2; budget -= 2; thatcher_rating += 4; right_dissent -= 10
face-image: img/events/hermes_1982.jpg

Within three days, the carriers Hermes and Invincible sail from Portsmouth to cheering crowds. Liners are requisitioned as troopships. Al Haig, the American Secretary of State, begins shuttling between London and Buenos Aires.

@negotiate
on-arrival: falklands = 5; thatcher_rating -= 12; right_dissent += 25; rebellion += 4; c2_con -= 3; c1_con -= 2

You agree to talks under American mediation. The islands will be under joint administration while their future is negotiated. The Commons hears it in near-silence, and then the right of the party erupts.

@war
title: The South Atlantic War
